 "research_notes": "Updated status after appraise iteration 3: Accepted and robust dataset associations now include MSI-high stronger WRN dependency (H5 validated; also MYC-high H53), SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H8; also MYC-high H54), and KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17; also MYC-high H55). New large accepted effect pending validation: TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency (H51, R31 estimate 0.802 [0.782,0.822]); validation requested. Registered context refinements for H51 across adenocarcinoma, high and low Cas9, high ROC, non-Avana library, and MYC-high cells. Rejected clinically meaningful directional hypotheses in this batch: H52 SMARCA4 loss with POLR2A dependency, H56 BRAF mutation with KRAS dependency, H58 KRAS mutation with weaker RIT1 dependency. Unresolved low-priority small/uncertain effects: H47 MSI-high DHX9, H48 MSI-high POLR2A, H49 MSI-high USP7, H50 MYC amplification MDM2, H57 KRAS mutation BRAF dependency. Next priorities: receive and assess H51 validation; if valid, decide whether context refinements are worth analysis. Do not request validation for weak MSI/MYC nulls. Continue to treat accepted effects as dataset-specific associations unless independent validation or external evidence supports broader claims.",
